## Program compliance
### iTrust Special Alt Doc — Option 2: 1099
Guideline: products/itrust/Special Alt Doc 04.27.26.pdf

Requirement | Required | Actual | Margin | Status
--- | --- | --- | --- | ---
Min FICO | 680 | 738 | +58 | ✅ Pass
Max LTV (Purchase, SFR) | 80% | 80% | 0% | ✅ Pass
Max DTI | 50% | 43.1% (locked CPA P&L method) | +6.9% | ✅ Pass
Reserves (PITIA) | 3 months | $11,130 needed; ~$137K personal after Vanguard liquidation | +$3.9K vs total cash needed | ✅ Pass
Trade lines | 3×12mo or 2×24mo | 4 tradelines, all >12mo | — | ✅ Pass
First-time homebuyer | Allowed | Yes | — | ✅ Pass
Credit events | None | None (clean file) | — | ✅ Pass
Citizenship | US Citizen | US Citizen | — | ✅ Pass
Property type | SFR allowed | SFR, 1 unit | — | ✅ Pass
1099 Tax Transcripts | Required | Not yet ordered | — | ⚠️ Pending
WVOE / YTD verification | Required | Not yet received | — | ⚠️ Pending
CPA letter (2-yr history) | Required | Expense-breakdown letter received 08/13 | — | ⚠️ Verify

Note: DTI is 43.1% under the LO-locked CPA P&L actual-expense method ($121,500/yr). The program's own 10% expense factor on most-recent-year 1099 yields $130,500/yr → 40.45% DTI (more favorable). A 25% standard factor would yield $103,875/yr → 50.4% (fail).

