### Income
**Qualifying income: $10,125/mo (LOCKED)** — CPA P&L actual-expense method per LO lock 08/13: 2-yr avg gross $138,500 − $17,000 actual expenses = $121,500/yr.

Method comparison (the decisive variable for this file):

| Method | Income/yr | Income/mo | Back-end DTI | 50% cap | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| CPA P&L actual expenses (LOCKED 08/13) | $121,500 | $10,125 | 43.1% | 50% | ✅ Pass |
| iTrust program 10% factor (most-recent yr) | $130,500 | $10,875 | 40.45% | 50% | ✅ Pass (most favorable) |
| 25% standard factor (AUS default risk) | $103,875 | $8,656 | 50.4% | 50% | ❌ Fail |

Calculation chain:
- 2025 1099s: Insight Global $85K + Kelly Services $42K + direct clients $18K = $145,000 gross — clients/chang/2-income/1099-nec-amazon-2025.pdf, clients/chang/2-income/1099-nec-microsoft-2025.pdf, clients/chang/2-income/1099-nec-others-2025.pdf
- 2024 1099 summary: $132,000 gross — clients/chang/2-income/1099-summary-2024.pdf. 2-yr avg gross = $138,500.
- CPA P&L: ~$17,000 actual annual business expenses; finalized 08/13 with breakdown of home office allocation, software/licensing, professional liability insurance — satisfies "verifiable business necessity." — clients/chang/2-income/cpa-profit-loss.pdf, clients/chang/6-notes/intake-update-0813.txt
- $138,500 − $17,000 = $121,500/yr = $10,125/mo — LOCKED method per LO. — clients/chang/6-notes/intake-update-0813.txt
- Program's own formula (iTrust Option 2): 10% factor on most-recent-year 1099 → $145,000 × 0.90 = $130,500/yr = $10,875/mo — more favorable than CPA P&L; both pass. — products/itrust/Special Alt Doc 04.27.26.pdf (p.8)
- 25% standard factor would fail: $138,500 × 0.75 = $103,875/yr → 50.4% DTI. LO locked CPA P&L method to prevent AUS defaulting to this. — clients/chang/6-notes/intake-update-0813.txt
- Income trending up +9.8% YoY (2024: $132K → 2025: $145K). — analyst:income-analyzer
- YTD may adjust income downward if WVOE shows lower earnings — products/itrust/Special Alt Doc 04.27.26.pdf (p.8)

